Message-ID: <94A10A1F8FF775439B2030F61DDDFA1AF7DCEC@gemini.amlin.com>




Dear Team,

 

Many thanks for posting this fantastic package, which has made my life
so much easier. I think there's a minor bug when dealing with filled
objects with NA borders, exemplified by the following R code:

 

frame()

rect(c(0,0.5),c(0,0),c(0.5,1),c(1,1),col=c('red','blue'),border=NA)

 

On most grDevices this produces two rectangles with no borders and no
space between them. On the tikz device there is a small white space that
I don't think should be there. A minor detail but it does spoil a couple
of graphs I've tried it with.

 

Regards,

 

Tom Day.

 

 



